«
@@ SensorPeriod — the period of an oscillation recorded by a sensor, with
@@ its standard uncertainty of type A.
@@ Level 1: the recording, as an array of rows [ t x y … ], the time t in
@@ seconds then one column per axis of the sensor, or the name of a CSV
@@ file of that form in the data directory, with or without a line of
@@ titles: the file exported by the application phyphox is read as it is.
@@ The axis with the largest signal is kept. Its zero crossings are located
@@ by linear interpolation, and confirmed once the signal has left the band
@@ of ±0.3 times its rms value, so that noise near zero adds none. Two
@@ straight lines of the same slope are then fitted to the times of the
@@ crossings, one for the rising and one for the falling ones: a constant
@@ offset of the sensor moves the two lines apart and leaves the slope, the
@@ period, unchanged. The standard uncertainty comes from the scatter of
@@ the crossings about these lines, with N − 3 degrees of freedom.
@@ Returns the period as T±σu, in seconds.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  If Dup TypeName "text" == Then Rcl End
  If Dup 1 Get 1 Get TypeName "text" == Then Tail End
  →Col →List
  → spcols
  «
    @ The times, then the axis with the largest sum of squares
    spcols 1 Get 0 0
    2 spcols Size For spk
      spcols spk Get Dup Dot
      → spss « If spss 3 Pick > Then Drop2 spss spk End »
    Next
    spcols Swap Get Swap
    → sptv spyv spss
    «
      spyv Size 1 Get
      → spnn
      «
        @ The threshold, the list of crossings, the side of the signal
        @ (0 at first), and the latest crossing seen
        spss spnn / √ 0.3 *
        { } 0 0
        → sphy sptc spst spcd
        «
          sptv 1 Get spyv 1 Get
          2 spnn For spk
            sptv spk Get spyv spk Get
            → spt0 spy0 spt1 spy1
            «
              If spy0 0 < spy1 0 < Xor Then
                spt0 spt1 spt0 - spy0 * spy0 spy1 - / + 'spcd' Sto
              End
              If spy1 Abs sphy > Then
                spy1 Sign
                → spsg
                «
                  If spsg spst ≠ Then
                    If spst 0 ≠ Then sptc spcd + 'sptc' Sto End
                    spsg 'spst' Sto
                  End
                »
              End
              spt1 spy1
            »
          Next
          Drop2
          If sptc Size 4 < Then "Too few oscillations" DoErr End
          @ The two lines of same slope: sums of squares and products
          0 0 0
          → spsxx spsxy spstt
          «
            1 2 For spj
              0 0 0 0
              → spcn spsm spsq spsj
              «
                spj sptc Size For spk
                  sptc spk Get
                  → sptk
                  «
                    spsj spcn sptk * + 'spsj' Sto
                    spsm sptk + 'spsm' Sto
                    spsq sptk Sq + 'spsq' Sto
                    spcn 1 + 'spcn' Sto
                  »
                2 Step
                spsxx spcn spcn Sq 1 - * 12 / + 'spsxx' Sto
                spsxy spsj spcn 1 - 2 / spsm * - + 'spsxy' Sto
                spstt spsq spsm Sq spcn / - + 'spstt' Sto
              »
            Next
            spsxy spsxx /
            spstt spsxy Sq spsxx / - 0 Max sptc Size 3 - / spsxx / √
            →σRange 1_s *
          »
        »
      »
    »
  »
»
